## Getting started

### Prerequisites

- A Mac with Xcode that supports the iOS 26 SDK
- A simulator or device running iOS 26 or later (the app uses the newer `Tab` API and tab bar accessory)

### Clone and run

```bash
git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/GasKurir.git
cd GasKurir
open GasKurir.xcodeproj
```

Then select an iPhone simulator (or your device) and press **Run** (`Cmd + R`).

No extra setup is required. At the moment the Home screen shows placeholder data from `BerandaViewModel`.

## Forking and contributing

Suggestions and bug reports are welcome through [Issues](https://github.com/USERNAME/GasKurir/issues). To work on your own copy:

1. **Fork** the repository using the Fork button at the top right of the GitHub page.
2. **Clone your fork**:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/GasKurir.git
   cd GasKurir
   ```
3. **Add the original repository as `upstream`** so you can pull future changes:
   ```bash
   git remote add upstream https://github.com/USERNAME/GasKurir.git
   ```
4. **Create a branch** for your change:
   ```bash
   git checkout -b feature/short-description
   ```
5. **Commit and push** to your fork:
   ```bash
   git add .
   git commit -m "Describe your change"
   git push origin feature/short-description
   ```
6. **Open a Pull Request** from your branch to `main` and describe what changed and why.

To keep your fork up to date:

```bash
git fetch upstream
git checkout main
git merge upstream/main
```

